      "review_notes": "The canonical target is UniformInt.law n. Complete residue blocks conserve arbitrary output credit for small targets; independent high/low digits flatten to one uniform rectangle for large targets. Each retry retains at least half of its source range. The program proof separates the equal, smaller and larger target cases; strong induction supplies a relative closed low-digit specification, and both retry loops use one direct conservation bound and factor-two amplification. Independent tests check source5/target2 residue rejection, deliberately conservative source6/target2 cutoff, recursive widths2\u21927\u21924\u21922, source3/target8 rectangle, equal-modulus native draws, singleton infinite off-support credit and generic framing."
    },
