      "review_notes": "The independent canonical law draws the negative-binomial total failure count, then allocates it with the standard multinomial PMF. Joint atoms factor at the returned count sum. The first-trial recurrence and categorical allocation identity yield one exact credit conservation lemma, including a remaining-success potential and fixed amplification1+p. Main CTE performs a supported categorical draw, decrements the remaining target or calls the pure indexed counter increment, then invokes its accumulator-universal induction hypothesis. Independent tests check a nonuniform joint count mass1/8, all-zero and absent failure categories, zero targets, infinite off-support credit, normalization and generic list-encoded resource framing."
    },
