      "review_notes": "The independent normalized color-word law exposes its explicit prefix product: remaining color count times odds, divided by current total weighted population. The Wallenius count law is its count pushforward; full-request support prevents overdraw. The two-color expectation is derived by identifying the categorical draw with the corresponding rational coin. Main CTE is finite draw-count induction, a supported selected-color coin, then the appropriate smaller urn call and optional marked increment. Independent unequal-odds tests use ones2/zeros1/odds3:1/n2: two marked draws have probability9/14, distinguishing Fisher3/5, while ordered mixed words have probabilities3/14 and1/7. Tests also cover zero draws without UniformInt, both empty-color boundaries, overdraw-zero mass, arbitrary infinite expectations and generic framing."
    }
